Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-25-2001||07:42 PM||||Ok, here's the deal.. yesterday I bought a t-top coupe as a project car.. took it to the mechanic, as it needed some work done in the engine bay.... (lots of rust around the battery tray.) I left it there, he was going to remove the wheels and wheel well liners, and have a look at the damage. He called me tonight, and said to come have a look at it.. there's more rust damage than I thought.. (I knew there could be substantial damage when I bought the car, I got a good deal on it)<P>The car has: <BR>-a good running 2.5L, fires right up, smooth idle<BR>-good tranny (auto)<BR>-good condition t-tops<BR>-good sail panels<BR>-good tail lights<BR>-passenger seat cover is good, drivers is ripped but stitched back up<BR>-tan interior, usual wear on the dash, console<BR>-red exterior, faded paint (body panels aren't perfect, but no major problems that I wasn't planning on altering anyway, ie. swapping to an aero front fascia)<P>The rust damage in the rear end is repairable, but it's gonna cost me.. the mechanic suggested I might be able to buy another (non-rusted) Fiero parts car, and graft the back end of that onto this one.. (the front of the frame is good, as far as we can tell)<P>The car already needs new brakes, and some other misc. work to pass safety. I also want to put on an 86 SE body and have the car repainted.<P>The question is... do you think it's worth it? I really like this car... I have about CDN $1,200 left in my budget, and I want to have it on the road by next summer.<P>I'll part this one out if I need to, but I really would like to restore it. I'm just not sure I can do everything I want within my budget. <B>Please, I need advice!!</B><P>btw, I'll get some pictures this week..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000001||PBJ||11-25-2001||08:46 PM||||hey, congrats on the T top fiero.  Rust is fixable. is your mech and fiero fan? or would he talk u out of any fiero?  Can u do any of the work yourself?||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||11-25-2001||08:57 PM||||Pete: yes, he likes Fieros... he didn't try to talk me out of it, he even recommended another mechanic who specialises in frame repair so I might have a better chance of getting the best repair possible. I'll probably get him to do the other repairs though<P>do you happen to know if there's any really cheap Fieros in the London area that might have a rust-free chassis? (don't care about the rest of it really)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-25-2001||08:58 PM||||I'm planning to do the interior & cosmetic stuff, but anything that's part of a safety system like the brakes, or something like the frame/engine cradle... I'll let a professional do.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
